2025-05-23 23:41:54,161 INFO Product development completed: {'pitch': CrewOutput(raw="Introducing the BMW Racing Block Set, an upcycled toy vehicle that seamlessly merges the thrill of BMW’s motorsport legacy with Lego's innovative building experience. This set features meticulously designed blocks made from recycled plastics, allowing children and adults alike to construct iconic BMW racing cars. Each model encapsulates the essence of high-performance engineering, complete with interchangeable components for customization, reflecting BMW’s passion for precision and craftsmanship.  \n\nThis collaboration leverages BMW’s identity of luxury, performance, and innovation alongside Lego’s commitment to creativity, fun, and sustainable play. The BMW Racing Block Set targets environmentally conscious families, young builders aged 6-12, and automotive enthusiasts, positioning itself as a green alternative in the toy market.  \n\nSustainability is at the heart of this product, emphasizing the use of upcycled materials to minimize environmental impact while promoting eco-friendly values to the next generation. The inherent storytelling potential is rich; it weaves a narrative of adventure, speed, and environmental responsibility, encouraging children to build their dream car while learning about sustainable practices.  \n\nThis co-branded opportunity positions both brands as leaders in innovation while fostering creativity, sustainability, and a sense of responsibility in play. Together, BMW and Lego can inspire future champions of both the road and the environment.", pydantic=None, json_dict=None, tasks_output=[TaskOutput(description='\n            Generate a pitch for an upcycled toy vehicle called "BMW Racing Block Set", a collaboration between BMW and Lego.\n            Include:\n            - A detailed concept (150-200 words)\n            - How it leverages each brand\'s identity\n            - Market positioning and intended audience\n            - Sustainability innov